  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.845083333333333,
      "text": "A number arrives at a costume party.",
      "source_sha256": "b8e8f3d5d52d09f63e2372b3a27146a0c7a892f8ccaa32e46cb187da300a6203"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.9650833333333333,
      "end": 8.421291666666667,
      "text": "Sometimes it wears digits, sometimes words, and sometimes a long addition sentence.",
      "source_sha256": "3ac254f0e83490824c89d87f60e16f7fda70e045fbe303201e71d9763e730971"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.541291666666666,
      "end": 11.881958333333333,
      "text": "Can we spot the same number beneath every disguise?",
      "source_sha256": "d043c7bd412d048c825257cbc0b28c3632c3bc99bb4fbabe17de1e1ea225dd1d"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.001958333333333,
      "end": 14.367541666666666,
      "text": "Let’s become number detectives.",
      "source_sha256": "c3f5a141cb391722bee03d63f3c876073a1cdbc9dd9fd5cd694a2ee5013f76fc"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.733333333333333,
      "end": 20.130583333333334,
      "text": "Today, we’re learning to read, write and regroup a whole number without changing its value.",
      "source_sha256": "f3c83e66bbcb9842b111aed8972cd0ee1181901dc2259b30b6751ce2737f651c"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.5,
      "end": 24.770791666666668,
      "text": "You’ll be able to match a number to its word form and expanded form.",
      "source_sha256": "5e83a172593669c245fa3b1b1c2f137253dc8d942ba21b95a33e58892b276a22"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.133333333333333,
      "end": 28.965333333333334,
      "text": "You’ll be able to explain how zero holds an empty place.",
      "source_sha256": "436c1f000c82f83435906e6688b90d9f34505e95dd7fa7c42e3fa43cddff41a3"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.333333333333332,
      "end": 33.71670833333334,
      "text": "You’ll be able to regroup thousands and hundreds to show the same amount.",
      "source_sha256": "add77c6019e931a5fcac4a2b6064262364a9b28b5a54b13c5be41baace093456"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.1,
      "end": 38.002541666666666,
      "text": "How can one number have several correct representations?",
      "source_sha256": "4cd0f45895c25be26b6d134293b97cc0090c68a5fcc35871be33f75dafc500a3"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.12254166666666,
      "end": 42.87266666666667,
      "text": "We can write its digits, say it in words, or split it into place values.",
      "source_sha256": "0d8b8ef80a81dac3669359bba3bfe6f4a675224b03ffacb83ee85fdccbcbd464"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.992666666666665,
      "end": 45.601125,
      "text": "All three describe the same quantity.",
      "source_sha256": "60c72dd6428bc72e7d43410615a2e1a362d996c70e7f81218b7f9d75bb3f84d0"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.721125,
      "end": 50.674791666666664,
      "text": "Let us represent four hundred and six thousand, two hundred and seventy five.",
      "source_sha256": "eaa99665ef7a168e28539f38289717f6b3741a1a091179eebe6d62b35e6e6213"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.03333333333333,
      "end": 54.659708333333334,
      "text": "How would you describe this number without using its digits?",
      "source_sha256": "99197661f37fc1b5c6bbc0706c87200ad07d07b72841d9a58482d479048f9122"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.77970833333333,
      "end": 58.983958333333334,
      "text": "Notice the empty ten-thousands place before we unpack the number.",
      "source_sha256": "643024ca702d2d84aedd26e2fe6f4ca05f2fe8420000ff6447b0619af02f7a85"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.5,
      "end": 62.70625,
      "text": "Start with the largest place.",
      "source_sha256": "7ae65a658d5e43144f3d89d3983d1a0e6e48fbed8d4d8004328bcf899062f638"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.82625,
      "end": 65.59425,
      "text": "The four means four hundred thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "d44df3423dd902329fc60eca253c0569b555ff93a7da2dcc9f19909c43496230"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.71425,
      "end": 69.004,
      "text": "The zero ten thousands contributes zero.",
      "source_sha256": "0f50d503c3dff05ce7743bc950db7bb967334d517855050a03e51ad41f776285"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.124,
      "end": 71.375875,
      "text": "The six means six thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "1255819809c7475bd522d759959fa1e903e1d6fd28ea3be3bdbbbc8c9acf5761"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.495875,
      "end": 78.44045833333334,
      "text": "Keep that zero as a placeholder when writing the standard number, so every other digit stays in the right place.",
      "source_sha256": "e42c43b2a47b177b8498e7ade674f1cc26c9489c329c085dd7fdc20fd9a5f048"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.8,
      "end": 82.82695833333334,
      "text": "Now add the smaller places: two hundred, seventy and five.",
      "source_sha256": "0accfbc903859f2d6ddf92b9a9235bd9456adebcf32aedbc021f0b8bf545f5a0"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.94695833333333,
      "end": 89.63020833333333,
      "text": "The expanded form is four hundred thousand, plus six thousand, plus two hundred, plus seventy, plus five.",
      "source_sha256": "6349c421fe9b1ebae80a4100334649a23bf3ba8c1e3dc61b10b15c59db5156bf"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.75020833333333,
      "end": 93.84641666666667,
      "text": "We can leave out the zero contribution without changing the total.",
      "source_sha256": "f35fef857ad10b8b6d93d648a969c8abd7316f836b771ba41fa3c5417a88a9a5"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.2,
      "end": 99.00191666666667,
      "text": "In words, say four hundred and six thousand, two hundred and seventy five.",
      "source_sha256": "3bfa800fd8d1cf432b29bb116000f92e524b132b45bf89411a07b857d61d8aa0"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.12191666666666,
      "end": 103.51416666666667,
      "text": "Notice how the thousands group and the final three digits fit together.",
      "source_sha256": "1e5f03fbde08a6ef389c323bd5a908f2a25f2faaee2019e90b9bc691a185850c"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.63416666666667,
      "end": 111.36566666666667,
      "text": "The word form, standard form and expanded form all represent four hundred and six thousand, two hundred and seventy five.",
      "source_sha256": "1e745ded1bee12276212fd86159ddd9519169fba971de17e11021aead3251aaa"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.73333333333333,
      "end": 115.90633333333334,
      "text": "Can we describe three thousand four hundred using only hundreds?",
      "source_sha256": "3e6494d7b67d739dd860c51ab001a0cc1ae3286244595231fb5adfea8d0996e2"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.02633333333333,
      "end": 119.442125,
      "text": "Predict how many hundreds would make the same amount.",
      "source_sha256": "0723eb05e08f2e617fd5efa96c990ddc9e2094297cf7e57cb69ee82208bcbe3d"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.96666666666667,
      "end": 123.38483333333333,
      "text": "We can also regroup a number.",
      "source_sha256": "7634c68abf308d32182d97d9b8c08254079359d93407d7bd0005bbe9d94a8d77"
    },
    {
      "start": 123.50483333333334,
      "end": 127.538375,
      "text": "Three thousand four hundred is three thousands and four hundreds.",
      "source_sha256": "446f60742c79c3a6c5b6a0de93310c14a69eca13cae8f9ddf8958e1a4f2c8343"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.658375,
      "end": 134.0275,
      "text": "It is also thirty four hundreds, because thirty four groups of one hundred make three thousand four hundred.",
      "source_sha256": "ae0dab56f88e0f69c40b38c4b56ede0d39a02c8339546f873f5a281eb7f3312e"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.1475,
      "end": 136.914375,
      "text": "The grouping changes; the amount does not.",
      "source_sha256": "8a2c8d7002e44b30773b05d9023dc40ee11f1ddab6cb236f13a954aabcdb3164"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.26666666666668,
      "end": 141.872375,
      "text": "It is tempting to erase the zero when writing the number in digits.",
      "source_sha256": "ae9fd8bebf330505a0a810052812d4e45965d6ebe70578778552c92e0c400386"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.992375,
      "end": 146.724,
      "text": "But removing that placeholder shifts the other digits into different places.",
      "source_sha256": "fd78b3a1bf3f9c85fa36fb17b06fb2b98981b7c0f08dd18e57c49dfbef92568d"
    },
    {
      "start": 146.844,
      "end": 153.53079166666666,
      "text": "Leave zero in the standard number, even when its zero contribution is omitted from expanded form.",
      "source_sha256": "1ee081473005eb44795d6ebb7374a05672f03217ada5ec2322db579cfa0b59cc"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.9,
      "end": 160.187125,
      "text": "What number is six hundred thousand plus twenty thousand plus four thousand plus three hundred plus eight?",
      "source_sha256": "a94b7fbef4de42d7d5d19910bbf9b5bba74870d86fca1d8bd2228e9e597b7531"
    },
    {
      "start": 165.2,
      "end": 169.724375,
      "text": "The total is six hundred and twenty-four thousand, three hundred and eight.",
      "source_sha256": "6651fe53f2b17fd2f5944dd64f72a3ec2984a24739bc74a714aee366d0f627c9"
    },
    {
      "start": 169.844375,
      "end": 171.5815,
      "text": "There are zero tens.",
      "source_sha256": "b0c8314fdd92ab2241bb2ca0c87e4bc1176edb6e5b61451cf4d0606ec19d53fc"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.93333333333334,
      "end": 177.972375,
      "text": "For practice, combine six hundred thousand, twenty thousand, four thousand, three hundred and eight.",
      "source_sha256": "6448d82796e6be71fcab4bbbe6d44c68d8b00d0ed9cf9e1fb384bd23e1b50ef7"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.092375,
      "end": 182.60683333333333,
      "text": "That gives six hundred and twenty four thousand, three hundred and eight.",
      "source_sha256": "559aaadfedadd21228d143c1b274242a27ec7273c608ebed9b2cb3dc6bfccfb6"
    },
    {
      "start": 182.72683333333333,
      "end": 186.30654166666667,
      "text": "There are no tens, but the zero still holds their place.",
      "source_sha256": "f2066d57593b263bf250551ad858d0d2dc486af78c7d4b2d5c7698c93de211cb"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.42654166666668,
      "end": 191.433625,
      "text": "Remember: read, partition and regroup, while keeping the value unchanged.",
      "source_sha256": "6ab908eead602d8726ecf3574031aaebc1ffa25771c9c5bb882fa11668c78a6e"
    },
    {
      "start": 191.8,
      "end": 196.766,
      "text": "Our goal was to read, write and regroup a whole number without changing its value.",
      "source_sha256": "fdaa2da06ea2d6325781b7425579cbcbc732e03dddbb937c66a4d3cfa9911d68"
    },
    {
      "start": 196.886,
      "end": 202.67866666666666,
      "text": "You can now explain your strategy, check the places carefully, and show why your answer makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "c05121d9be0181e7d5e9eabc7bfda5690a466e386fdea17c2467447b05a9070e"
    },
    {
      "start": 202.79866666666666,
      "end": 206.41195833333333,
      "text": "Choose a number of your own and explain it to someone nearby.",
      "source_sha256": "cab9c866b98aa8f683275d69424690577f29ddc91a2d7762edd1880e714e1e0e"
    },
    {
      "start": 206.53195833333334,
      "end": 209.71975,
      "text": "Then try the lesson practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "bd3e5c67a871736d618226bff00bea66256633ab7b5cb23f1df99fed1c7327c5"
    }
  ],
